{
  "version": 1,
  "_comment": "VDL Mode 2 reception — monitors ALL SEVEN European VDL2 channels SIMULTANEOUSLY (136.700, 136.725, 136.775, 136.800, 136.900, 136.925, 136.975 MHz) via the vdl2 plugin's multi-channel mode.  All seven channels sit within 275 kHz, well inside the 2 MHz capture bandwidth, so a single tuning at 136.837 catches every burst on every channel — no missed messages.  D8PSK at 10.5 kSym/s ≈ 31.5 kbit/s, ~24 kHz wide bursts, HDLC/AVLC framing.  Antenna: any 137 MHz antenna + SAWbird+NOAA passes this range cleanly.  bw_hz 2 MHz is the HackRF minimum.  Gain 32 is a starting point — dial up if the constellation-view donut is faint, dial down if it looks like a chunky blob (compression).",
  "center_hz": 136837500.0,
  "bw_hz": 2000000,
  "gain_db": 32.0,
  "gain_auto": false,
